The n=13 separation was a SAMPLING ARTIFACT — the 4 probe rows happened to be
high-score4 Shimano 4-arm chainrings.  Full cohort shows enormous variance
within XL42+ (many near zero — likely Campagnolo 5-arm, hidden spider behind
cogset, occluded by cogset behind chainring, ramp-lined inner faces).

Predicate sweep — (bestN==4 ∧ score4>τ4) OR (bestN==5 ∧ score5>τ5):
  τ4 ∈ {0.10, 0.12, 0.14, 0.16, 0.18, 0.20, 0.22}
  τ5 ∈ {0.10, 0.15, 0.18, 0.20, 0.22, 0.25, 0.30}
  Result: NO cell meets AC1 Wilson 95% UB ≥ 80% AND AC2 cog_FP = 0.

  At every operating point that hits enough XL42+ rows for AC1≥80% UB, the
  predicate also fires on currently-correct cog rows (LOSS).  At every cog-FP=0
  operating point, XL42+ hit rate < 25% (W95UB ≪ 80%).

  The OR-arm structure means: tightening τ4 to suppress 11T 4-fold outliers
  also suppresses many XL42+ 4-fold hits; tightening τ5 to suppress Small/Mid
  5-fold loses Campagnolo 5-arm XL chainrings.

XL42+ rows with low score (12 lowest):
  Half are correct (FFT got the right tooth count anyway — abstain unnecessary)
  Half are confidentWrong (the AC1 target).  Even at score4>0.0 the AC1 target
  rows have score4 in 0.020-0.111 range.  No τ4 separates them from cog
  outliers.

VERDICT:

  Option A (Hough on raw RGBA):  all 4 variants overlap on n=13.  Exhausted.
  Option C (bolt-pattern):       no AC1 W95UB ≥ 80% + AC2 = 0 cell on n=145.
                                 Exhausted.

  The geometric/symmetry discriminator layer on raw RGBA is structurally unable
  to separate chainrings from cogs on this corpus at the QA Wilson 95% UB ≥ 80%
  bar (per PAP-1091 precedent).  The previous FFT-magnitude prior ladder
  (PAP-1100/PAP-1108) also closed at this bar.

REMAINING PATHS for PAP-1481:

  Option B (operator-aim authoritative): treat aim-circle radius as ground
    truth for outer gear radius; lock peakR := aimR; re-derive tooth count
    from circumference.  PAP-1484 confirmed there is no pitch/circumference
    constant in gearCounter.js — would need new pitch-derived rule, OR a
    look-up table from {chainring, cog} families.  HIGH UX RISK (operator
    misaim → confident-wrong predictions).  Not endorsed by PAP-1484 / 1488.

  Option D (descope PAP-1481 wontfix): file PAP-1481 closed wontfix at the
    geometric-discriminator layer; PAP-758 has no orthogonal escape route
    available with current corpus + Wilson UB bar.  Surviving in-regime path
    is PAP-1480 (joint R×tc scoring, PAP-1102 lineage) — accept that some
    chainring confident-wrongs cannot be discriminated and rely on tc
    co-evidence to dampen the score.

Recommendation: post n=145 evidence to PAP-1489 cross-check #3; ask QA to
endorse DESCOPE both Option A and Option C; suggest closing PAP-1481 wontfix
with handoff comment to PAP-1480 lineage.
